1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,890
A queen's throne came from a far-off land... before an eye could blink.

2
00:00:04,940 --> 00:00:10,210
Who could do that? And what would you say, if it were yours?

3
00:00:10,260 --> 00:00:13,890
This is the story of Prophet Sulaiman, alayhis salaam.

4
00:00:13,940 --> 00:00:16,540
The King Who Was Grateful.

5
00:00:17,840 --> 00:00:23,070
Who was Prophet Sulaiman, alayhis salaam, and what did Allah give him?

6
00:00:23,120 --> 00:00:28,849
He was the son of Prophet Dawud, alayhis salaam, the king of Bani Israil.

7
00:00:28,899 --> 00:00:32,252
Allah says: "And to Dawud We gave Sulaiman.

8
00:00:32,302 --> 00:00:38,330
An excellent servant, indeed he was one repeatedly turning back to Allah."

9
00:00:38,380 --> 00:00:46,702
Allah tells us of a case they judged: a people's sheep had gone into a field at night and eaten its crop.

10
00:00:46,752 --> 00:00:52,550
Prophet Dawud, alayhis salaam, judged, and Prophet Sulaiman, alayhis salaam, judged too.

11
00:00:52,600 --> 00:01:01,930
And Allah says: "We gave understanding of the case to Sulaiman, and to each of them We gave judgement and knowledge."

12
00:01:01,980 --> 00:01:08,400
Understanding from Allah: that was the first gift. It would not be the last.

13
00:01:09,700 --> 00:01:17,170
"And Sulaiman inherited Dawud." Prophet Sulaiman, alayhis salaam, became prophet and king after his father.

14
00:01:17,220 --> 00:01:27,067
And he made a dua: "My Lord, forgive me, and grant me a kingdom such as will not belong to anyone after me.

15
00:01:27,117 --> 00:01:29,906
Indeed, You are the Bestower."

16
00:01:29,956 --> 00:01:32,710
He asked for forgiveness first. Then for the kingdom.

17
00:01:32,760 --> 00:01:34,511
And Allah answered.

18
00:01:34,561 --> 00:01:43,050
"So We subjected to him the wind, blowing by his command, gently, wherever he directed."

19
00:01:43,100 --> 00:01:47,207
A morning's journey on that wind was a month's travel.

20
00:01:47,257 --> 00:01:50,330
An evening's journey was another month.

21
00:01:50,380 --> 00:02:04,870
And Allah made a spring of molten copper flow for him, and some of the jinn worked for him by his Lord's permission: high palaces, great bowls like reservoirs, cooking pots fixed to the ground.

22
00:02:04,920 --> 00:02:10,614
But with all of it came one command: "Work, O family of Dawud, in gratitude.

23
00:02:10,664 --> 00:02:13,677
And few of My servants are grateful."

24
00:02:13,727 --> 00:02:20,100
Few are grateful. Would Prophet Sulaiman, alayhis salaam, be one of the few?

25
00:02:21,400 --> 00:02:31,862
Prophet Sulaiman, alayhis salaam, said to his people: "O people, we have been taught the language of birds, and we have been given from all things.

26
00:02:31,912 --> 00:02:34,510
Indeed, this is evident bounty."

27
00:02:34,560 --> 00:02:42,710
Not "I earned it." Not "I am great." Evident bounty: a gift, from Allah.

28
00:02:42,760 --> 00:02:44,396
Remember those words.

29
00:02:44,446 --> 00:02:50,739
Because later in this film, a man who was given wealth will say the opposite...

30
00:02:50,789 --> 00:02:53,890
and we will see where each one ended.

31
00:02:53,940 --> 00:03:03,510
And so his army gathered: "And gathered for Sulaiman were his soldiers of the jinn, and men, and birds, and they were marching in rows."

32
00:03:03,560 --> 00:03:09,000
One day, that army marched toward a valley... and one tiny ant spoke.

33
00:03:10,300 --> 00:03:16,540
What would you do, if an army that size was coming toward your home?

34
00:03:16,980 --> 00:03:30,437
"Until, when they came upon the valley of the ants, an ant said: O ants, enter your dwellings, that you not be crushed by Sulaiman and his soldiers, while they perceive not."

35
00:03:30,487 --> 00:03:33,444
One small ant. She warned her people.

36
00:03:33,494 --> 00:03:41,751
And she even made an excuse for the army: "while they perceive not." They would not mean to harm you.

37
00:03:41,801 --> 00:03:45,391
And Prophet Sulaiman, alayhis salaam, heard her.

38
00:03:45,441 --> 00:03:48,971
"So he smiled, amused at her speech."

39
00:03:49,021 --> 00:03:54,491
A king with the wind and the jinn at his command... smiled at the words of an ant.

40
00:03:54,541 --> 00:03:56,368
And then he made a dua.

41
00:03:56,418 --> 00:04:09,754
Save this one: "My Lord, enable me to be grateful for Your favour which You have bestowed upon me and upon my parents, and to do righteousness of which You approve.

42
00:04:09,804 --> 00:04:14,704
And admit me, by Your mercy, among Your righteous servants."

43
00:04:14,754 --> 00:04:18,462
He did not ask for more power. He asked to be grateful.

44
00:04:19,201 --> 00:04:23,061
But one bird in his army... was missing.

45
00:04:24,360 --> 00:04:29,525
Prophet Sulaiman, alayhis salaam, inspected the birds.

46
00:04:29,575 --> 00:04:35,070
"Why do I not see the hoopoe, or is he among the absent?"

47
00:04:35,120 --> 00:04:39,619
A king who notices one small bird missing.

48
00:04:39,669 --> 00:04:47,760
He said the hoopoe would be punished, unless it brought a clear reason.

49
00:04:48,700 --> 00:04:50,950
Then the hoopoe came back.

50
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:58,124
"I have encompassed in knowledge that which you have not encompassed, and I have come to you from Sheba with certain news."

51
00:04:58,174 --> 00:05:01,881
What news could a bird bring to a prophet?

52
00:05:03,180 --> 00:05:13,717
"Indeed, I found a woman ruling them, and she has been given of all things, and she has a great throne."

53
00:05:13,767 --> 00:05:19,170
A rich land. A great throne. A strong army.

54
00:05:19,220 --> 00:05:25,477
"I found her and her people prostrating to the sun instead of Allah."

55
00:05:25,527 --> 00:05:32,442
A whole people, bowing to the sun. The sun that Allah Himself had made.

56
00:05:32,492 --> 00:05:36,723
Prophet Sulaiman, alayhis salaam, did not send an army.

57
00:05:36,773 --> 00:05:42,330
He said: "We will see whether you were truthful, or were of the liars."

58
00:05:42,380 --> 00:05:44,221
And he wrote a letter.

59
00:05:45,520 --> 00:05:49,786
"Take this letter of mine and deliver it to them.

60
00:05:49,836 --> 00:05:54,297
Then leave them, and see what answer they return."

61
00:05:54,347 --> 00:05:55,977
The letter reached the queen.

62
00:05:56,027 --> 00:06:01,941
She called her chiefs: "O eminent ones, indeed to me has been delivered a noble letter.

63
00:06:01,991 --> 00:06:10,168
Indeed, it is from Sulaiman, and indeed, it reads: In the name of Allah, the Entirely Merciful, the Especially Merciful.

64
00:06:10,218 --> 00:06:14,083
Be not haughty with me, but come to me in submission."

65
00:06:14,133 --> 00:06:20,690
Her chiefs said: we are strong, we are fighters, but the decision is yours.

66
00:06:20,740 --> 00:06:32,010
She said: "Indeed, kings, when they enter a city, they ruin it, and render the honoured of its people humbled." She feared what kings do.

67
00:06:32,060 --> 00:06:38,480
"I will send them a gift, and see with what the messengers return."

68
00:06:39,056 --> 00:06:45,600
A gift of wealth... to a man Allah had given everything. How would he answer?

69
00:06:46,900 --> 00:06:50,660
The messengers arrived with the queen's treasure.

70
00:06:51,140 --> 00:06:57,655
And Prophet Sulaiman, alayhis salaam, said: "Do you provide me with wealth?

71
00:06:57,705 --> 00:07:03,345
But what Allah has given me is better than what He has given you.

72
00:07:03,395 --> 00:07:07,303
Rather, it is you who rejoice in your gift."

73
00:07:07,353 --> 00:07:10,190
He sent them back with it.

74
00:07:10,240 --> 00:07:13,670
And the queen set out herself, to come to him.

75
00:07:13,720 --> 00:07:20,580
Then Prophet Sulaiman, alayhis salaam, asked his court something that sounds impossible.

76
00:07:21,880 --> 00:07:32,150
"O assembly, which of you will bring me her throne before they come to me in submission?"

77
00:07:32,200 --> 00:07:42,897
A powerful one of the jinn said: "I will bring it to you before you rise from your place, and indeed, I am for this task strong and trustworthy."

78
00:07:42,947 --> 00:07:47,027
Before you stand up. That was the jinn's offer.

79
00:07:47,898 --> 00:07:55,083
But one who had knowledge from the Scripture said: "I will bring it to you before your glance returns to you."

80
00:07:55,133 --> 00:07:57,240
Before your eye can blink.

81
00:07:58,000 --> 00:08:03,763
And there it was. The queen's great throne, from Sheba, placed in front of him.

82
00:08:03,813 --> 00:08:09,600
Now remember the question from the start: what does a man say when Allah gives him everything?

83
00:08:10,176 --> 00:08:19,893
Prophet Sulaiman, alayhis salaam, said: "This is from the favour of my Lord, to test me whether I will be grateful or ungrateful.

84
00:08:19,943 --> 00:08:24,360
And whoever is grateful, his gratitude is only for himself.

85
00:08:24,410 --> 00:08:30,390
And whoever is ungrateful, then indeed my Lord is Free of need and Generous."

86
00:08:30,440 --> 00:08:36,640
A throne from a far-off land, in a moment... and his first thought was: this is a test.

87
00:08:39,220 --> 00:08:42,531
When the queen arrived, she was shown a throne.

88
00:08:42,581 --> 00:08:47,290
"Is your throne like this?" She said: "It is as though it was it."

89
00:08:47,340 --> 00:08:49,976
Then she was told to enter the palace.

90
00:08:50,026 --> 00:08:53,771
When she saw it, she thought it was a body of water.

91
00:08:53,821 --> 00:08:57,038
But it was "a palace made smooth with glass."

92
00:08:57,088 --> 00:09:03,393
Her throne carried in a blink. A palace of glass she took for water.

93
00:09:03,443 --> 00:09:07,581
And a king who gave everything to Allah.

94
00:09:08,161 --> 00:09:12,261
And the queen, who used to bow to the sun, said:

95
00:09:12,701 --> 00:09:21,904
"My Lord, indeed I have wronged myself, and I submit with Sulaiman to Allah, Lord of the worlds."

96
00:09:21,954 --> 00:09:28,971
She did not submit to Sulaiman, alayhis salaam. She submitted with him, to Allah.

97
00:09:29,021 --> 00:09:37,821
A letter, a gift sent back, and a grateful heart: that is how a queen turned from the sun to her Creator.

98
00:09:39,120 --> 00:09:44,234
Prophet Sulaiman, alayhis salaam, ruled in gratitude.

99
00:09:44,284 --> 00:09:49,110
And then came the one thing no kingdom can stop.

100
00:09:49,160 --> 00:09:59,710
"And when We decreed for him death, nothing indicated to the jinn his death except a creature of the earth, eating his staff."

101
00:09:59,760 --> 00:10:07,280
He was still leaning on his staff, and the jinn kept working, not knowing he had passed away.

102
00:10:08,200 --> 00:10:09,630
"But when he fell..."

103
00:10:09,680 --> 00:10:17,160
"Then it became clear to the jinn that if they had known the unseen, they would not have remained in humiliating punishment."

104
00:10:17,560 --> 00:10:22,526
The jinn, who offered to bring a throne before a man could stand up...

105
00:10:22,576 --> 00:10:26,200
did not know the unseen. Only Allah knows it.

106
00:10:27,500 --> 00:10:34,225
Allah gave Prophet Sulaiman, alayhis salaam, a kingdom no one will ever have again.

107
00:10:34,275 --> 00:10:37,630
And the word he kept saying was: thanks.

108
00:10:37,680 --> 00:10:38,926
Remember Qarun?

109
00:10:38,976 --> 00:10:48,234
He was given treasure and said: "I was only given it because of knowledge I have." The earth swallowed him.

110
00:10:48,284 --> 00:10:55,502
Prophet Sulaiman, alayhis salaam, was given far more, and said: "This is from the favour of my Lord."

111
00:10:55,941 --> 00:10:59,104
Same test. Two answers.

112
00:10:59,154 --> 00:11:13,771
So today, look at one thing Allah gave you: your health, your family, your home, and say his dua: "My Lord, enable me to be grateful for Your favour."

113
00:11:13,821 --> 00:11:22,349
Which part of the story of Prophet Sulaiman, alayhis salaam, amazed you most: the ant, the hoopoe, or the throne?

114
00:11:22,399 --> 00:11:24,621
Tell us in the comments.

115
00:11:24,861 --> 00:11:29,791
Next week: Prophet Ibrahim, alayhis salaam, thrown into a fire...

116
00:11:29,841 --> 00:11:33,391
and the one command that made it cool and safe.

117
00:11:33,441 --> 00:11:40,133
Until then, watch the full movies of Prophet Musa and Prophet Yusuf, alayhimas salaam...

118
00:11:40,183 --> 00:11:41,102
links below.
